         <Description>The Hinode Solar Optical Telescope Filtergraph (SOT-FG) Level 0 FGSIQUV FITS data product contains uncalibrated Stokes I, Q, U, and V image arrays acquired in the shutterless full-Stokes observing mode. The product is identified by DataCode FGSIQUV and OBS_TYPE='FG shutterless Stokes', distinguishing it from the shuttered FGIQUV product. Each inspected FITS Primary HDU contains a three-dimensional array with four image planes for Stokes I, Q, U, and V. Shutterless readout enables rapid polarimetric imaging over a restricted field of view; the image dimensions and angular pixel scales depend on observing settings. The FITS headers identify the product with GEN_ID=33 and generally report FGMODE='shutterless'. The observing passband and its wavelength offset are recorded by the FITS keywords WAVE and WAVEOFF. The Level 0 images precede ground-based scientific calibration.</Description>
